WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 5 - Limited Lines

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.140
Now, straighten your legs!

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.170
One, two, three!

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.260
One, two, three!

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:47.080
Huh? You over there!

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.110
This isn't karate!

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:50.580
Do it again!

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.530
One, two, three!

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.440
One, two, three!

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:08.740
Make sure you bring your text fees by next week.

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:15.150
Everything costs money.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:19.300
I was accepted into this school thanks to Ms. Tsukikage...

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:23.550
and she's already lending me money for tuition....

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:26.280
I don't want to cause her any more trouble.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.280
Really?!

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.240
Yeah.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.910
That park's always really crowded on Sundays.

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:34.090
They need someone badly.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.780
I'll mention you to them.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.290
Thank you!

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:45.050
How much longer will my hot dog and sandwich take?

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:45.120
Hut o' Refreshment

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:46.720
Here it is! Sorry it took so long!

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:49.960
Can I put in an order?

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:51.380
Yes, I'll be right there...

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.480
Sakurakouji...

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:03.360
Wow, you've left home and found a job?

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.660
You're working really hard!

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.360
Oh... it's nothing...

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.140
I just like working, so...

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.970
I'm not really very good at organizing things...

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:11.840
Thank you for the meal.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.470
How are your lessons going?

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:16.330
Not great. I'm always getting yelled at.

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:19.980
If we were in the same theater group, we'd be in the same class.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:23.050
I'll come again.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.590
Walk forward.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:35.180
Okay! You just stepped on a discarded nail!

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:39.430
Ouch! Ow! Ow!

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:41.820
What are you doing over there?

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.780
You just stepped on a nail!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:49.260
Yes... that's why I'm looking at the sole of my foot...

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.370
You were looking... at the sole of your foot?

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:55.140
Yeah, I was thinking "wow, that was a big nail I just stepped on."

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:57.980
You need to take this class more seriously!

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.940
Now, let's move onto expressions.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.640
We'll start with laughter.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:03.900
Right, everyone - laugh!

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.040
Hey, you!

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.540
It's that girl again...

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.520
You must take part too!

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:19.060
But... I <i>was</i> laughing.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.490
You called that laughter?!

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.070
I want everyone to pay attention!

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:24.070
Your facial expressions are too frail!

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:25.530
I'm sorry.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.700
Why did <i>she</i> get a scholarship?

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.010
We're so much better than she is!

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:33.720
What was up with her during that laughter exercise?

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.820
And the nail exercise, for that matter...

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:44.850
Why? Why is Ms. Tsukikage listening to them...

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.480
bash Maya and smiling?

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.960
Next week, we'll debut our much anticipated first play.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:51.670
Really?

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:54.860
I want you to memorize these lines before then.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.000
Yes. No. Thank you. Excuse me.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.430
We're making a play out of these lines?

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.940
What is she planning?

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:14.600
It's raining.

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:21.920
It's started to rain.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.310
That reminds me...

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.270
Want some candy?

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:32.040
Note: The word for candy and rain are the same, "ame," with only a difference in stress.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.040
Candy... Rain!

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:35.500
They're the same word...

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:38.440
They sound the same, but they mean different things...

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:41.260
The inflection of the words... the stress is different.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:46.210
The difference is so small, yet it changes the meaning so completely.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:51.880
I've never noticed it before because, until now, I used words without thinking...

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:54.340
Maya...

00:05:57.570 --> 00:06:00.810
You sweep a room... you put on slippers.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:03.670
You write a paper... you scratch your head.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.490
Even though the words sound the same,

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:09.220
the slight change in emphasis completely changes their meanings.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.250
Could this word also be... Yes! It is!

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:15.080
That must be it!

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:19.980
It's like she's possessed or something.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.480
She's scary.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.130
What?

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:26.220
I said she's scary.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:28.620
She's figured it out.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:32.540
That girl has figured out how important words are, beyond just simply acting them.

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:34.330
She did it instinctively!

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.390
What are you saying?

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:39.450
You don't really believe she's a natural, do you?!

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.890
I've heard what everyone's been saying about her.

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:44.030
That's why it's so scary!

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:45.080
I mean, listen:

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:47.970
When the teacher told us to act as if we'd stepped on a nail,

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:50.290
she didn't explicitly tell us to act as though it had hurt us.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:55.100
When we did that laughter exercise, our teacher didn't explicitly tell us to laugh out loud.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:03.870
That's the easiest way to express laughter, sure, but...

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:06.280
what she was doing was also laughter!

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:11.600
She followed the instructions based on her reaction to the words themselves.

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:15.090
That meant a slight upturn of her lips,

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:17.590
or merely raising her leg a touch.

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:22.510
When she told her to do it, her body moved instantly.

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:24.280
That's called instinct!

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:25.770
Instinct?

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:28.650
You mean she responded to the words according to her animal instincts?

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:32.030
That girl sure is something.

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:34.000
Maya!

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.090
Two sandwiches please!

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:39.890
Yes. No. Thank you. Excuse me.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:42.930
I wonder what kind of play we'll put on using only these words.

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:43.850
<i>Maya</i>!

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.670
I said I need two sandwiches!

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:47.110
Yes, right away!

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:48.760
And table five wants a coke!

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:52.380
Here you go!

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:57.170
Today, I came on my own to see you.

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:59.450
But I guess I shouldn't hassle you while you're working.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.050
No, not at all!

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:03.800
What's that?

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.660
Oh, it's a poster!

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:08.210
I got it from the Daito Theater's box office.

00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:10.290
The White Rose Wife

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:11.280
Oh wow!

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.330
Ayumi's going to be in it too?

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.030
I'd love to go see that!

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:18.360
Can I go with you?

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.690
I'll sit in the corner and be ever so quiet!

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:21.830
Please!

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:34.580
The private screening for the new film is at half past six this afternoon.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:35.890
I'll definitely be there.

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:40.620
Before that, there's a meeting about the theater's schedule for fall.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.360
That's at the hotel in Akasaka, isn't it?

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:43.860
I'll head there shortly.

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:46.770
Could you please sign this document?

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:49.480
This is the New Year's shoot for next year, right?

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:53.620
Mr. Masumi is really something, isn't he?

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:58.420
Even though the Daito Corporation won't be under his control for a while,

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:00.440
he's already starting to put in the legwork.

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:05.410
Ever since he was a little boy, he's had a strict specialist education...

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:07.830
at the behest of his father.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:12.520
Which is why he's been able to represent his father without hesitation...

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:15.140
ever since he was struck down with illness and confined to his home.

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:16.960
He really is a remarkable worker.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:21.180
He's so young and handsome and yet, he probably has no time for dating.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:23.470
He's not like normal people!

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:27.300
He's following in the footsteps of his father!

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:37.530
This place is packed with famous actors!

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.060
This is so amazing!

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:44.170
Well, this is the studio at Daito Theater - this is pretty normal.

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:49.250
"I know why they call you the White Rose Wife!"

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:53.760
"You're beautiful and pure like a white rose..."

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:59.660
"But your thorns draw crimson blood from anyone who dares to touch you."

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:01.800
Ayumi is so good.

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:03.480
She really is astonishing.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.340
Her voice projects so clearly.

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:08.290
And her presence is awe-inspiring.

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:12.980
It's that girl again...

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:18.990
This is... Looks like this one's been mixed in by mistake.

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:21.620
I didn't realize roses could be this color.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.390
Oh hello, Masumi.

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:25.090
Ah yes...

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:28.040
Actually, this color is a throwback.

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:35.340
In the Eighteenth Century, European noblemen regularly staged rose competitions.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:38.040
They competed to breed flowers with a variety of new colors,

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:40.390
but nobody managed to grow a blue rose.

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:43.660
Roses don't have the correct pigments to produce the color blue.

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:49.170
So what they finally created was a color that wasn't quite blue - a purple rose.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:51.550
So this is that throwback, huh?

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:02.760
Okay everyone! Take ten!

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:03.500
Yes, sir!

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:04.560
Oh, hi Masumi!

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.850
Have you come to watch, Mr. Masumi?!

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:11.950
Didn't I meet you at Ondine?

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:13.120
Y-Yes!

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:14.790
My name is Maya Kitajima!

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:16.910
The Daito Theater Studio

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:19.910
I see you've done it again, Mr. Masumi!

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:19.910
You're... in the Tsukikage Troupe?

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:26.380
So that means you might one day play the Scarlet Angel too.

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:28.860
The Scarlet Angel?

00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:30.250
That's right.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:33.080
The forgotten masterpiece, <i>The Crimson Angel</i>...

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.540
featured Chigusa Tsukikage's finest role.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:40.040
My mother was one of the many actresses who wanted to play the lead role,

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:43.150
but Ms. Tsukikage refuses to relinquish the rights to it,

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:45.420
and no one else can play the role at present.

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:50.620
She formed the Tsukikage Acting Troupe in order to personally train an actress...

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:52.470
to be capable of playing the Scarlet Angel.

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:54.200
Which means...

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:58.320
someone in the Tsukikage Troupe will get to play the role...

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:01.020
of the Scarlet Angel at some point.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:05.800
Looks like this could get interesting!

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:11.100
Hey, you! How did you meet Chigusa Tsukikage?

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:16.290
Can you tell us what she's been doing since she retired from the acting world?

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:18.580
Is she seeing anyone?

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:27.030
This isn't the type of place where people can just walk around and watch.

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:28.350
Please leave now.

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:30.090
Okay!

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:33.310
This way, please. You too, Sakurakouji.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:37.260
I can't believe Mr. Masumi is actually defending that girl...

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:55.010
Right! I want each of you to step onto the stage, one at a time.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:08.340
One of the most important aspects of acting is listening and responding...

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:09.680
to the people who speak to us.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:12.470
Even when using the same words,

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:15.060
there are countless nuances we must use in response.

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:18.460
You are all playing passersby.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:21.690
As the owner of this house, I will say a number of things to you.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:28.340
Anyone who uses unassigned words or doesn't respond in an appropriate manner will fail the test.

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:29.980
What does she mean by "appropriate"?

00:13:29.980 --> 00:13:32.730
Naitou, you begin.

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:39.950
You're walking down a street! Look more natural!

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:45.440
My, if it isn't Yousuke!

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:46.320
Y-Yes!

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:48.730
Don't you remember me?

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:49.600
No...

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:51.250
Is your father doing well?

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:52.010
Yes!

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:56.250
We have to use the exact same words to express different meanings.

00:13:56.490 --> 00:14:00.420
By putting different emotions into our voices, the meaning of the words change!

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:01.940
I'm not prepared.

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:04.050
There's something stuck to your coat.

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:05.370
Huh? Where?

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:06.130
Failed!

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:09.440
You look as pretty as ever, Miss Yayoi!

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:11.010
Well, of course!

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:12.270
Failed!

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:22.500
It's Ayumi Himekawa!

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:23.830
Ayumi!

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:27.980
Why on earth is that starlet here?

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:37.340
My name is Ayumi Himekawa.

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:42.800
I've been told that my mother, Utako Himekawa, was your apprentice.

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:44.670
Pleased to meet you.

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:46.730
To what do I owe the pleasure of this visit today?

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:50.880
I'm currently studying acting in a troupe by the name of Ondine.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:54.860
I would like to observe this lesson, if possible.

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:56.760
Or is that too much to ask?

00:14:57.190 --> 00:14:59.460
Not at all.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:02.670
Then, I have another request, Ms. Tsukikage.

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:06.650
May I take the stage in place of the teacher?

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:11.680
She's come to spy on us!

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:15.010
She wants to find out what kind of group we are!

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:17.630
Any failure will tarnish the whole troupe!

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:19.000
That's fine.

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:22.120
Maya Kitajima, step forward.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:26.500
Ms. Tsukikage, I don't think she can do this task...

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:29.100
Maya, hurry up and get on the stage!

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:30.610
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:32.720
What should I do?

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:57.390
I wonder why our teacher picked her...

00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:59.490
She's going to fail on the first question.

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:01.420
Begin!

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:05.880
Welcome!

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:08.590
I've been waiting for you, so why don't you come in?

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:10.040
Y-Yes!

00:16:12.350 --> 00:16:13.310
Would you like some coffee?

00:16:13.310 --> 00:16:14.940
Or do you prefer tea?

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:15.860
Co-

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:18.900
Which would you like?

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:23.850
No....

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:27.900
My, my. You don't like either?

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:29.080
Yes.

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:37.650
Have some milk then.

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:39.240
Thank you.

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:40.730
How many sugars do you take?

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:41.750
Tw-

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:44.420
No.

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:46.840
Are you telling me you don't like sugar either?

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:49.810
Damn her!

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:51.980
But Maya's really hanging in there!

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:53.840
She's picking her words carefully!

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.450
Hey, hurry up!

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:57.460
Hurry up!

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:01.840
There's a girl duking it out with Ayumi Himekawa!

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:03.120
Really?

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.200
Let's go watch!

00:17:05.590 --> 00:17:07.150
I don't believe it.

00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:10.230
She only has four lines she can use, but they've been at it for an hour now!

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:11.790
A whole hour?!

00:17:13.820 --> 00:17:15.570
If she carries on like this,

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:18.920
Miss Ayumi "National Treasure" Himekawa will be humiliated.

00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:20.750
Go, Maya!

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:23.850
Go, Maya!

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:27.530
Ms. Tsukikage... this is...

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:32.580
Everyone's cheering for me.

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:34.960
This has never happened before.

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:36.530
This is the first time anything like this has ever happened to me!

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:40.730
I was always made fun of and couldn't do anything right...

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:43.090
Even my mother made fun of me...

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:46.380
Watch this...

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:48.620
Now she's going down!

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:57.350
Hey... what's the name of your principal?

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:59.040
Her name?

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:01.010
Answering "yes" or "no" wouldn't make sense.

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:04.550
If I can't say her name, I have to say that I don't know it.

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:13.840
She just shook her head, but that's a response!

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:16.940
Which means she's still only used those four words!

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.740
Well, this is very odd.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:22.400
How can you not know the name of your own principal?

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:24.860
She just transfered here recently!

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:26.770
It's perfectly normal that she doesn't know it!

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:28.100
That's right!

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:32.530
It looks like I got out of that one.

00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:34.640
But what will she ask me next?

00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:36.530
Do you like music?

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:38.630
Yes.

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:40.510
I'll put some music on then.

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:42.270
I have all kinds of music.

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:47.990
So, what kind of music do you like?

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:49.700
What kind of music?!

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:51.890
I can't answer that!

00:18:55.140 --> 00:18:56.930
Shaking my head won't work this time.

00:18:57.890 --> 00:19:00.340
What should I do?

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:03.100
I guess she won't make this one.

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:08.070
Come on, I want to put on a song you like!

00:19:08.070 --> 00:19:09.610
What kind of music do you like?

00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:13.310
I'm stuck...

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:23.620
What's up with this girl?

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:27.380
There's no way she can respond to that using only her four lines!

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:49.800
What's she doing?

00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:53.820
She's miming looking for a CD!

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:05.940
She found one!

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:08.320
She found a CD she likes!

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:18.010
Thank you.

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:20.810
We'll stop there.

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:24.730
Thank you very much, Ayumi Himekawa.

00:20:24.730 --> 00:20:26.740
You did a good job too, Maya.

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:28.780
We'll end today's lesson here.

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:31.420
She did it!

00:20:34.350 --> 00:20:36.370
Maya, you were great!

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:38.610
You had me on the edge of my seat!

00:20:38.610 --> 00:20:40.990
You got so far with just four words!

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:47.000
I look forward to seeing your group develop, Ms. Tsukikage.

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:59.370
Now I can see why she gave that girl a scholarship.

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:09.880
I think this is the first time I've been cornered to such an extent.

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:16.110
Maya Kitajima, we might end up fighting on stage someday.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:21.430
Everyone is being so friendly to me.

00:21:21.430 --> 00:21:24.650
I'm so glad I made it into this troupe!

00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:28.900
Mother... I really like acting.

00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:31.950
It makes me feel like there's something that even I can be good at.

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:33.240
Little old me!

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:37.650
That was the moment she felt that she wanted to live in the world of acting...

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:40.010
That she could achieve something there.

00:21:40.010 --> 00:21:45.990
But Maya had no way of knowing that the stairs she must climb...

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:49.270
would be surrounded by the searing flames of war.

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
Gomennette iwaretara

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
When you say "I'm sorry,"

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
Anata wo semerarenai yo

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
I can't blame you.

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
Sonna watashi wo kitto shitterundeshou

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
I'm sure you know that's how I am.

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
Nee zurui yo

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
That's not fair.

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Yasashisa ni damasaretatte

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Even if I'm being fooled by kindness,

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
Anata nara isso iito shinjita

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
I believed that with you, it might be worth it.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Sayonara wa doushite itoshiindarou

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Why are goodbyes so precious,

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
Hanareteyuku noni

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
even though they mean we're separating?

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
Ushinatta ondo wo oboeteruyo

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
I remember how it got colder.

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
Yurushitai dakara anata

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
I want to forgive you, so please don't go.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Ikanaide douka ikanaide

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Whatever you do... just don't go.

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:26.280
Maya, you're obsessed with acting even when you're on a date!

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:30.580
I understand your desire to get up on stage as soon as you can, but at least look at me.

00:23:31.860 --> 00:23:35.280
I heard that the Tsukikage Acting Troupe will be staging <i>Little Women</i>.

00:23:35.670 --> 00:23:37.730
I'm happy you've been cast as Beth.

00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:41.540
But you're not the only one who wants to be on stage.

00:23:41.840 --> 00:23:44.370
You'll lose your role if your acting seems superficial.

00:23:44.760 --> 00:23:48.510
Will you be able to grasp the true essence of Beth?

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 6 - My Beth
